g showing Soto tied or ahead, or a softer national environment for Republicans, would move the race back toward a tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Newest usable poll is 47 days old; polling uncertainty inflated.", "Incumbent Darren Soto (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Democratic incumbent Darren Soto faces Republican Dan Green in this Republican-leaning Central Florida district, one of the cycle's top House targets. The district's partisan lean points Republican, and the 2026 national environment adds to that edge, offsetting part of Soto's incumbency advantage. Seven of ten race raters call the seat a Lean or Likely Republican flip, three rate it a Tossup, and Roll Call has labeled Soto the nation's most vulnerable House Democrat.\n\nSoto holds clear financial advantages, raising $3.5 million to Green's $2.2 million with far more cash on hand, and the DCCC has joined the airwaves while more than 25 unions back him. The only public poll, a Democratic-sponsored August survey, showed the race tied at 41 percent. The combined weight of ratings, markets, and fundamentals points to a narrow Republican edge.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.3442, "margin": -2.38}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2846, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.2806, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.3778, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.2308, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.3096, "margin": -2.6}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.3559, "margin": -2.6}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.3413, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.3329, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.2822, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.28, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.2817, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.2782, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.2318, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.2308, "margin": -4.0},